"sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"T000193","fullName":"Rep. Thompson, Bennie G. [D-MS-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MS"},{"bioguideId":"V000081","fullName":"Rep. Velázquez, Nydia M. [D-NY-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"E000296","fullName":"Rep. Evans, Dwight [D-PA-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"W000808","fullName":"Rep. Wilson, Frederica S. [D-FL-24]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"J000309","fullName":"Rep. Jackson, Jonathan L. [D-IL-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"C001059","fullName":"Rep. Costa, Jim [D-CA-21]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"C001072","fullName":"Rep. Carson, André [D-IN-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T23:02:39+00:00","id":"hr5816-119","introducedDate":"2025-10-24","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-10-24","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Education and Workforce."},"laws":[],"number":"5816","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Education","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001130","district":30,"fullName":"Rep. Crockett, Jasmine [D-TX-30]","party":"D","state":"TX"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-10-24","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Halting Education Loan Payments during Federal Employment Disruptions Act or the HELP FEDs Act</strong></p><p>This bill waives late fees, penalties, and other adverse actions for federal employees who miss student loan payments during a lapse in appropriations (i.e., government shutdown). &nbsp;</p><p>The bill applies to education loans made, insured, or guaranteed under the Higher Education Act of 1965, including loans held by the Department of Education (ED) or contracted loan servicers.</p><p>Under the bill, a federal employee who misses a student loan payment that is due during a period of involuntary disruption of pay (i.e., the employee did not receive scheduled wages due to a lapse in appropriations) may not be assessed a late fee or penalty or be subject to other adverse actions. The bill also prohibits federal employees from incurring additional interest on such loans during an involuntary disruption of pay.&nbsp;</p><p>In addition, the bill requires ED to coordinate with credit reporting agencies and loan&nbsp;servicers to ensure that no adverse information related to delayed or missed student loan payments of a federal employee during an involuntary disruption of pay is furnished to any consumer reporting agency.&nbsp;</p><p>The bill applies retroactively to any involuntary disruption of pay occurring on or after October 1, 2025.&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-10-29T16:40:13Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"HELP FEDs Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2025-11-18T09:05:17Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-11-18T09:05:17Z"}
